{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2658","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2658","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2658\",\"parent_revision\":\"c1f736588f84ecda084beedd414f4743acf82409ad40d145196928a390466819\",\"root_revision\":\"c1f736588f84ecda084beedd414f4743acf82409ad40d145196928a390466819\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-07-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe `add-new-feature` skill documents that `sam_plan(action='create', issue=N)` auto-registers the task-plan artifact on the linked GitHub issue. This holds for the monolithic path (tasks passed at create time) but not for the incremental drafting path (create with empty tasks \u2192 append_task \u2192 finalize).\\n\\nObserved today: an agent built a 23-task plan using the incremental path and verified post-finalize that no task-plan artifact was registered. The agent then manually registered it, which conflicts with the documented rule (\\\"do NOT call artifact_register for the task-plan type\\\"). The agent then had to archive the registration to signal it was not authoritative, leaving a stale artifact entry.\\n\\nImpact: agents using the incremental path either leave the artifact unregistered (breaking discoverability) or register it manually (breaking the single-writer contract). Both outcomes create downstream confusion for orchestrators and validators.\\n\\nThe fix is either: trigger artifact auto-registration at finalize time on the incremental path, or document explicitly that the incremental path requires a separate registration step and update the skill accordingly.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **sam_plan incremental path does not auto-register task-plan artifact** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session transcript \u2014 swarm-task-planner agent working on plan Pe7547575 (2026-06-19)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-06-19\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-06-20)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-07-10T08:08:53.069178Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA SUMMARY (re-assessment, 2026-07-10 \u2014 scoped to the user-confirmed residual gaps only)\\n\\nGoal:\\n- Close the two residual acceptance-criteria gaps left open by the 2026-07-10 staleness review: add a regression test under `sam_schema/tests/` covering the incremental `sam_plan` path (AC5), and add an explicit test proving `GistTaskLayer.finalize_plan` is idempotent when called twice on an already-finalized plan (AC6). The original defect (missing artifact registration) is SUPERSEDED by commit 6ac6e37 (#2662) \u2014 this goal is narrower than the item's original title.\\n\\nSuccess Output:\\n- New/updated pytest test(s) closing AC5 and AC6, passing under `uv run pytest`.\\n\\nConditions (reverse prerequisites):\\n1. AC5 test location is legitimate | Requires: confirmation `sam_schema/tests/` is a valid, collected location for a Gist/GistTaskLayer-scoped test despite its current beads-only content | Why: AC5's literal wording names this directory; if it were merely a typo the fix would target the wrong file.\\n2. AC6 scenario and expected assertions | Requires: trace of what \\\"no duplicate entries or error\\\" concretely means across the three cooperating no-op guards | Why: AC6 must assert a specific, provable outcome, not a vague non-regression.\\n3. Test fixture reuse vs duplication | Requires: knowledge of whether `sam_schema/tests/conftest.py` fixtures collide with the Gist-layer fakes needed for the new test | Why: avoids fixture name collisions or unnecessary reinvention.\\n4. CI actually collects the new test | Requires: confirmation no `testpaths` restriction excludes `sam_schema/tests/` from the run | Why: a test that CI never runs does not close AC5.\\n5. Scope stays narrowed (no re-litigating AC1-4) | Requires: confirmation AC1-4 are already MET | Why: prevents scope creep back into re-verifying settled criteria.\\n6. Real (non-fake) `store()` idempotency guard exists | Requires: confirmation the production `ArtifactRegistryClient.store()` \u2014 not just the test double \u2014 actually skips the manifest PATCH on repeat calls | Why: AC6's \\\"no duplicate manifest entries\\\" claim rests on this, not just on the local no-op guard.\\n\\nVerification:\\n- Condition 1: Evidence=AVAILABLE | Disposition=N/A | Basis: Staleness Context entry (2026-07-10, user-confirmed) explicitly states \\\"add a unit/integration test satisfying AC5's literal sam_schema/tests/ location requirement (or duplicate the tests_sam coverage there)\\\" \u2014 the user already resolved the directory question; no further clarification needed.\\n- Condition 2: Evidence=EVIDENCE-DERIVED | Disposition=N/A | Basis: Read `sam_schema/core/backends/local_yaml.py:603-632` \u2014 `finalize_plan` has a no-op guard (`if plan.state == PlanState.READY: return` at line 624-625, no write). Read `sam_schema/core/gist_task_layer.py:1069-1100` \u2014 `GistTaskLayer.finalize_plan` delegates to local (no-op on 2nd call) then unconditionally calls `_write_through`. Read `_write_through` (lines 708-746) \u2014 content-hash `.sha256` sidecar dedup (`_write_through_content_unchanged`, lines 647-667) skips the Gist upload when content is unchanged, which it will be since local finalize was a no-op. Contradiction check: no code path found that would re-upload or error on a content-identical second call \u2014 inference holds.\\n- Condition 3: Evidence=AVAILABLE | Disposition=N/A | Basis: Read `sam_schema/tests/conftest.py` in full \u2014 contains only `_FakeBdRunner` and beads-specific fixtures (`fake_runner`, `plan_id_and_runner`, etc.), no Gist-related names. Read `tests_sam/test_gist_write_through.py:41-157` \u2014 `_InMemoryArtifactStore`, `_make_fake_client`, `gist_layer` fixture are self-contained and importable/duplicable without collision.\\n- Condition 4: Evidence=AVAILABLE | Disposition=N/A | Basis: `pyproject.toml:403-418` `[tool.pytest.ini_options]` \u2014 no `testpaths` key; `addopts` restricts only by marker (`-m \\\"not e2e and not cross_backend\\\"`), not by path. Default rootdir-wide discovery collects both `sam_schema/tests/` and `tests_sam/`.\\n- Condition 5: Evidence=AVAILABLE | Disposition=N/A | Basis: Staleness Context entry (2026-07-10) cites `uv run pytest tests_sam/test_gist_write_through.py -k \\\"finalize or append_task\\\" -q` \u2192 4 passed, and explicitly marks AC1-AC4 MET with per-criterion reasoning already recorded.\\n- Condition 6: Evidence=AVAILABLE | Disposition=N/A | Basis: Read `sam_schema/core/artifact_registry_client.py:117-157` directly \u2014 `store()` builds `manifest = provider.get_manifest(issue)`, checks `entry_exists` by matching `artifact_type`/`artifact_id`/`status`, and skips `_artifact_registry.register(...)` + `provider.set_manifest(...)` when already present (lines 144-156). This is the real production guard, not only the test double's behavior.\\n\\nDecision:\\n- APPROVED\\n\\nAssumptions to Confirm (EVIDENCE-DERIVED only):\\n- Condition 2's inference (double-finalize is a full no-op end-to-end, so AC6 documents existing-correct behavior rather than a defect) | Basis: static code trace of three cooperating guards (local no-op, content-hash dedup, manifest entry-exists check) | Validation step: the new AC6 test itself is the validation \u2014 write it to assert zero manifest-entry growth and no exception on the second `finalize_plan` call; if it fails, the inference was wrong and there is an actual idempotency defect to fix, not just a coverage gap.\\n\\n<concerns>\\nStale or misleading documentation\\n  Observation: Backlog item #2658's \\\"Resources\\\" and original \\\"Desired Structure\\\" sections (written 2026-06-20) list `sam_schema/tests/` as \\\"Test target\\\" without noting it is a beads-only directory unrelated to GistTaskLayer/Gist tests \u2014 an assumption later corrected only informally in the 2026-07-10 Staleness Context free text, not in the Resources/AC sections themselves.\\n  Why it matters: A future agent reading only the top-level Acceptance Criteria/Resources (without reading the full Staleness Context prose) could duplicate an entire Gist-layer fixture stack into a directory whose conftest.py and existing tests are all beads-scoped, creating a confusing, orphaned test module with no clear ownership.\\n  Blocks current work: No \u2014 the 2026-07-10 user decision already resolves which directory to use.\\n  Recommended owner/destination: backlog grooming / documentation hygiene.\\n  Recommended follow-up: When implementing AC5's test, add a short module docstring in the new `sam_schema/tests/` file explaining why a Gist-layer test lives in a nominally beads-scoped directory (cite this item and the literal-AC-wording rationale), so the next reader is not confused.\\n\\nTech debt introduced knowingly\\n  Observation: Satisfying AC5 by duplicating (rather than relocating) tests_sam/test_gist_write_through.py's fixture stack (_InMemoryArtifactStore, _make_fake_client, gist_layer) into sam_schema/tests/ creates two independently-maintained copies of the same GistTaskLayer test doubles.\\n  Why it matters: A future change to GistTaskLayer's constructor or ArtifactRegistryClient's interface would require updating both fixture copies; missing one silently leaves stale/broken test doubles that pass for the wrong reasons.\\n  Blocks current work: No.\\n  Recommended owner/destination: backlog follow-up item.\\n  Recommended follow-up: Consider a small shared fixture module (e.g. `sam_schema/tests/_gist_fakes.py` or promoting the fakes to a repo-wide test-utils module) if a third consumer of these fakes appears; not worth doing for two call sites today.\\n</concerns>\\n</div>\\n\\n### Artifact Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-20T08:14:23.338183Z</sub>\\n\\n- Primary artifact type: Bug fix\\n- Behavioral boundary: `artifact_list(item_id=N, artifact_type='task-plan')` returning a non-empty result with finalized content after a complete incremental plan build (create with `tasks=[]` + N `append_task` calls + `finalize`).\\n- Domain-semantic evaluation target: Acceptance criteria must prove the single-writer contract holds (no manual `artifact_register` call needed or valid) and that `artifact_list` returns a registered entry with the finalized plan content after the incremental path completes.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-20T08:14:43.331518Z</sub>\\n\\n1. Identify a GitHub issue number `N` in a repo with `GITHUB_TOKEN` set and SAM MCP server active (GistTaskLayer path \u2014 not memory backend).\\n2. Call `sam_plan(action='create', slug='test-incremental', goal='Test incremental path', tasks=[], issue=N)` \u2014 creates a drafting plan, returns `plan_id`.\\n3. Call `sam_plan(plan=<plan_id>, action='append_task', task={id: 'T1', title: 'Test task'})` one or more times.\\n4. Call `sam_plan(plan=<plan_id>, action='finalize')`.\\n5. Call `artifact_list(item_id=N, artifact_type='task-plan')`.\\n6. Expected: count \u2265 1 with a `CURRENT` entry whose content (via `artifact_read`) contains the finalized plan YAML (`state=ready`, all tasks present).\\n7. Observed (session Pe7547575, 2026-06-19): no `task-plan` artifact entry visible after finalize.\\n\\nNote: must be run against the live GitHub backend since `ArtifactRegistryClient` only performs Gist operations when `GistTaskLayer` is active.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-20T08:15:13.604949Z</sub>\\n\\n- Session transcript evidence: agent working on plan Pe7547575 (2026-06-19) \u2014 swarm-task-planner built a 23-task plan via incremental path, verified post-finalize that `artifact_list` returned no `task-plan` entry, then manually registered via `artifact_register`, then archived the stale entry.\\n- Source: `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/gist_task_layer.py` \u2014 `finalize_plan` (line 941) calls `_write_through` (updates Gist content) but does NOT call `store()` to register or refresh the manifest entry.\\n- Source: `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/artifact_registry_client.py` \u2014 `store()` (line 117) registers the manifest entry AND uploads content; has idempotency guard at lines 148\u2013156 (skips manifest PATCH if entry already exists, but still uploads content).\\n- Source: `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/gist_task_layer.py` \u2014 `create_plan` (line 167) calls `self._artifact_client.store(issue=issue, content=yaml_content)` unconditionally when `issue` is set, regardless of whether `tasks` is empty.\\n- Key code gap: `_write_through` (called by `finalize_plan`) updates Gist file content but does NOT trigger a manifest entry registration. If the manifest entry was created at `create_plan` time, it persists \u2014 but the content registered remains the drafting skeleton. If `create_plan` Gist write failed, no entry exists at all.\\n- Skill documentation at `add-new-feature/SKILL.md` lines 486\u2013488 and 570 contradicted by observed behavior.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-20T08:15:30.200803Z</sub>\\n\\n7/10 \u2014 P1 is appropriate. The incremental path is the required path for plans with 16+ tasks (documented in CLAUDE.md), so all large plans are affected. The bug breaks the single-writer contract documented in both CLAUDE.md and `add-new-feature/SKILL.md`, causes stale artifact entries, and silently undermines plan discoverability for orchestrators and validators.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-20T08:15:48.457175Z</sub>\\n\\n- Blocks: Orchestrators and validators that depend on `artifact_list(artifact_type='task-plan')` to discover plans \u2014 they cannot find plans built via the incremental path.\\n- Bottleneck: Single-writer contract violated when agents manually register `task-plan` artifacts to work around the gap, creating stale or duplicate entries that confuse downstream `artifact_read` calls.\\n- Affected agents: `@dh:swarm-task-planner` (produces large plans via incremental path), `@dh:plan-validator`, `@dh:feature-verifier`, `@dh:implement-feature` (reads `task-plan` artifact to locate the plan).\\n- Documentation contradicted: CLAUDE.md and `add-new-feature/SKILL.md` both state \\\"do NOT call artifact_register for the task-plan type\\\" but agents are forced to do exactly that to recover from the gap.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-20T08:16:06.644658Z</sub>\\n\\n- Restores the single-writer contract: agents using the incremental path no longer need to manually register or archive stale entries.\\n- Enables plan discoverability via `artifact_list` for all plans, regardless of which path was used to build them.\\n- Eliminates the stale artifact entry pattern observed in session Pe7547575.\\n- Reduces orchestrator confusion and downstream errors in `implement-feature`, `work-backlog-item`, and plan validators that rely on `artifact_list`.\\n- Makes the incremental path behavior identical to the monolithic path from the caller's perspective.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-20T08:16:24.498316Z</sub>\\n\\nAfter `sam_plan(action='finalize')` completes on a plan created via the incremental path with `issue=N` set at create time:\\n\\n1. `artifact_list(item_id=N, artifact_type='task-plan')` returns count \u2265 1 with an entry whose status is `CURRENT`.\\n2. The entry's content (via `artifact_read`) reflects the finalized plan YAML \u2014 `state=ready`, all appended tasks present \u2014 not the empty drafting skeleton uploaded at create time.\\n3. No manual `artifact_register` call is needed or valid for the `task-plan` type on this path.\\n4. Behavior is identical to the monolithic path (`sam_plan(action='create', tasks=[...], issue=N)`).\\n</div>\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-20T08:16:53.284736Z</sub>\\n\\nTwo fix options exist \u2014 both valid, one preferred:\\n\\n**Option A (preferred \u2014 code fix):** Modify `GistTaskLayer.finalize_plan` (`sam_schema/core/gist_task_layer.py` line 941) to call `self._artifact_client.store(issue=issue, content=<finalized_yaml>)` after the local finalize write and `_write_through` call. The idempotency guard in `store()` skips the manifest PATCH when the entry already exists (registered at create time), so this is safe. The Gist content is updated to reflect the finalized plan regardless. This makes the finalized state visible to `artifact_list` with authoritative content after finalize.\\n\\n**Option B (documentation fix only):** Update `add-new-feature/SKILL.md` and CLAUDE.md to document that the incremental path requires a manual registration step at finalize time, clarify the \\\"do NOT call artifact_register\\\" rule as monolithic-path-only. Lower-risk but leaves the single-writer contract broken and behavior inconsistent across paths.\\n\\nFix target: `GistTaskLayer.finalize_plan` in `sam_schema/core/gist_task_layer.py`.\\nTest target: `sam_schema/tests/` \u2014 new test confirming `artifact_list` returns an entry after the incremental path completes.\\nDocumentation target (either option): `add-new-feature/SKILL.md` lines 486\u2013488 and 570, CLAUDE.md GistTaskLayer section.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-20T08:17:12.425997Z</sub>\\n\\n1. Given a plan created via `sam_plan(action='create', tasks=[], issue=N)` followed by one or more `append_task` calls and `sam_plan(action='finalize')`, `artifact_list(item_id=N, artifact_type='task-plan')` returns count \u2265 1 with a `CURRENT` status entry \u2014 identical to the monolithic path.\\n2. Given the finalized incremental plan, `artifact_read(item_id=N, artifact_type='task-plan')` returns YAML content where `state=ready` and all appended tasks are present \u2014 not the empty drafting skeleton uploaded at create time.\\n3. No manual `artifact_register` call is needed or valid for the `task-plan` type on either the monolithic or incremental path \u2014 the \\\"do NOT call artifact_register for the task-plan type\\\" rule holds unconditionally on both paths.\\n4. The monolithic path (`create_plan` with a non-empty `tasks` list and `issue=N`) continues to produce the same artifact registration behavior as before \u2014 no regression.\\n5. A unit or integration test in `sam_schema/tests/` confirms criterion 1 by calling the full incremental sequence against a mock artifact client and asserting the manifest entry exists and has finalized content after `finalize`.\\n6. `GistTaskLayer.finalize_plan` is idempotent: calling `finalize` twice on an already-finalized plan does not create duplicate manifest entries or raise an error.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-20T08:17:36.973282Z</sub>\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Source | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/gist_task_layer.py` \u2014 `create_plan` (line 167), `finalize_plan` (line 941), `_write_through` |\\n| Source | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/artifact_registry_client.py` \u2014 `store()` (line 117), idempotency guard (line 148) |\\n| Source | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 `_sam_plan_create` (line 328), `_sam_plan_finalize` (line 509) |\\n| Source | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/action_models.py` \u2014 `CreatePlanConfig.issue` field description (line 201) |\\n| Skill | `/dh:add-new-feature` \u2014 Phase 4 note on auto-registration (lines 486\u2013488, 570) |\\n| Docs | `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 GistTaskLayer write-through section, prohibited patterns |\\n| Backlog | #2590 \u2014 related: GistTaskLayer triggers GitHub API write on every `sam_task` state change (same write-through layer) |\\n| Test dir | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/tests/` |\\n</div>\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-20T08:17:53.740276Z</sub>\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 the fix is self-contained within `GistTaskLayer.finalize_plan` and optionally documentation files.\\n- Blocks: None currently tracked; unblocks correct plan discoverability for all orchestrators using the incremental path.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-20T08:18:12.555787Z</sub>\\n\\n- No deterministic reproduction test exists yet \u2014 the observed failure is from a session transcript (Pe7547575, 2026-06-19), not a repeatable command sequence. A reproduction step against the live or mock GistTaskLayer should confirm the failure mode before implementing the fix.\\n- Two candidate failure modes remain unresolved: (a) `finalize_plan` does not call `store()`, so the manifest content stays as the drafting skeleton and `artifact_list` returns the entry but `artifact_read` returns stale content; (b) `create_plan(tasks=[], issue=N)` Gist write failed in the specific session, leaving no manifest entry at all. The fix for (a) differs from the fix for (b). Code trace suggests (a) is more likely since `finalize_plan` never calls `store()`, but (b) cannot be ruled out without a reproduction.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-20T08:18:29.043536Z</sub>\\n\\nSmall \u2014 The fix is a single method modification in `GistTaskLayer.finalize_plan` to add a `store()` call after the existing `_write_through`. The idempotency guard in `store()` prevents double-registration. A unit test asserting the post-finalize artifact manifest entry is the main verification artifact. Documentation updates to `add-new-feature/SKILL.md` and CLAUDE.md are minimal. Total scope: 1 source file change, 1 new test, 2 documentation files. Preceded by a reproduction step to confirm the failure mode.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Staleness Context\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-07-10T08:05:14.772277Z</sub>\\n\\nStaleness detected 2026-07-10: functional commits since groom date 2026-06-20.\\n\\nPhase 1 (git log --after=2026-06-20 --diff-filter=AMRD on Impact-Radius/Resources files) found 4 functional commits: 9d4479b, 6ac6e37, 653635b, c4f556b.\\n\\nPhase 2 drift-assessment classification: SUPERSEDED. Commit 6ac6e37 (fix(sam_schema): fix incremental plan artifact registration and linting violations (#2662), 2026-07-08) is a near-verbatim fix of this item's title. Root cause per the agent's read: `CreatePlanConfig.issue` already supported auto-registering the task-plan artifact via `ArtifactRegistryClient.store()` at create time regardless of `tasks` being empty \u2014 the actual defect was that CLAUDE.md's documented incremental workflow told agents to call `sam_plan(action='create', tasks=[])` without `issue=`, producing a local-only plan that never registers. 6ac6e37 fixes exactly that (CLAUDE.md step 1 now requires `issue=<github_issue_number>` at create time).\\n\\nAC verification against current HEAD + passing tests (`uv run pytest tests_sam/test_gist_write_through.py -k \\\"finalize or append_task\\\" -q`, 4 passed):\\n- AC1 MET \u2014 create-time store() registers the manifest CURRENT entry regardless of tasks length.\\n- AC2 MET \u2014 `tests_sam/test_gist_write_through.py::test_finalize_plan_persists_to_gist` exercises the exact incremental sequence (create tasks=[] issue=N -> append_task x2 -> finalize) and passes; content is state=ready with both tasks, not the drafting skeleton.\\n- AC3 MET \u2014 no code path calls artifact_register manually for task-plan type (grep confirmed); consequence of AC1/AC2 plus corrected docs.\\n- AC4 MET \u2014 monolithic path and server.py unchanged in substance (only cast()->_require_plan() and de-nested-import refactors); same tests pass.\\n- AC5 UNMET \u2014 test literally required under `sam_schema/tests/`; actual regression coverage lives in top-level `tests_sam/test_gist_write_through.py`, a different directory. `sam_schema/tests/` only covers the beads backend.\\n- AC6 NOT VERIFIED \u2014 `LocalYamlTaskProvider.finalize_plan` has a no-op guard for already-READY plans and `_write_through`'s content-hash dedup should prevent duplicate registration/errors on a second finalize, but no test explicitly calls finalize_plan twice to confirm.\\n\\nDecision (user-confirmed 2026-07-10): do not close as superseded. Keep item open, narrow remaining scope to the two residual gaps only: (1) add a unit/integration test satisfying AC5's literal sam_schema/tests/ location requirement (or duplicate the tests_sam coverage there), (2) add an explicit test asserting GistTaskLayer.finalize_plan is idempotent when called twice on an already-finalized plan (AC6).\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"dc88623191fc5dfa5f62de928e16cc6d02abbe1fcb88f87a028ae52f8b94f1ed\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCJJgA\"}"}